---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_92",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 92,
  "text": "<p> [[360.13]] <b>93. JOHANN HEINRICH PAPE AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[360.14]] Lüneburg, 1. (11.) Dezember 1690. [92.97.]</b></p>\n<p> [[360.21]] Vir Excellentissime, Amplissime, Consultissime, </p>\n<p> [[360.22]] Patrone omni observantiae cultu suspiciende. </p>\n<p> [[360.23]] O fortunatum diem illum, quo Excellentiam Tuam compellare ac de facie nosse mihi\n[[360.24]] contigit! Cujus quidem felicitatis etsi dudum particeps fieri optaverim, factus tamen non sum\n[[360.25]] nisi aliquot demum abhinc mensibus, cum non modo humanissime exciperer, sed etiam ex\n[[361.1]] doctissime disserentis ore ita penderem, ut multum inde fructus in me redundaverit. Et quamlibet\n[[361.2]] ex eo tempore non semel in animo habuerim, quodam epistolio Tuam Excellentiam\n[[361.3]] salutare, in primis ut gratias pro exhibita coram promissaque benevolentia persolverem; pudore\n[[361.4]] tamen nescio quo prohibitus, quicquid illud est officii, de tempore in tempus distuli. Quid igitur\n[[361.5]] obvenire mihi potuisset optatius, quam literae, Tuae Excell. manu honoratissima ad me exaratae?\n[[361.6]] (quantumvis per quendam patruelium meorum, Juris Licentiatum et Practicum, ob\n[[361.7]] nullum extrinsecus apparens praenomen, meis ingratiis resignatae) quibus factum, ut, quod\n[[361.8]] antea verebar ne alicujus audaciae ac temeritatis incusaretur, id nunc si omitterem, summae\n[[361.9]] ingratitudinis ac incivilitatis notam effugere non possem. Praecipue vero gratulor mihi de\n[[361.10]] possessione istius libri, qui ipsum Dn. Autorem suum latuit hactenus, ad me vero hac pervenit\n[[361.11]] occasione: Kirchneri cujusdam, bibliopolae quondam Lipsiensis, cum obiisset, ob concursum\n[[361.12]] creditorum per annos bene multos delituerant libri, donec tandem quatuor ferme abhinc annis\n[[361.13]] ex decreto judicii consensuque creditorum concurrentium per modum auctionis publicae distraherentur.\n[[361.14]] Inter quos cum decem circiter exemplaria praesentis operis extarent, fiebat, ut et\n[[361.15]] mihi licitanti unum ex his addiceretur, sed mancum et mutilum in plagula titulo destinata. Id\n[[361.16]] quod deprehendens postea, desiderio habendi pleni operis, alium quendam emtorem eo inducebam,\n[[361.17]] ut suum mihi exemplar, quod acceperat integrum, cederet. Atque sic bina possedi\n[[361.18]] hactenus exemplaria. Quod non absque fato ita contigisse crediderim, ut scilicet plurimum juris\n[[361.19]] in istum librum, quippe partum suum, habenti, horum alterutrum traderem vel potius restituerem,\n[[361.20]] nec tamen ipsemet isto quasi thesauro carerem propterea. Cui quidem fini alterum illud\n[[361.21]] exemplar, murium nescio an aliam quandam injuriam expertum, ita praeparandum a bibliopega\n[[361.22]] curavi, ut, quae in eo desiderabantur, ex altero, quod ligatum habeo, supplere potuerim. Ite ergo\n[[361.23]] folia, et doctrina admirabili, et ingeniositate incomparabili refertissima, ite, inquam, ad parentem\n[[361.24]] vestrum, verumque adeo dominum, jure optimo maximo vos vindicantem a me, qui\n[[361.25]] duntaxat bonae fidei possessor appellandus sum, Autorique ac Domino vestro circa jus suum\n[[361.26]] firmius in id, quod casu quopiam amiserat, controversiam movere nequeo. Sed et juvate me in\n[[361.27]] exorando eum, ut suum in me inclinet favorem, et ex pristinis moralibus juridicisque meditationibus,\n[[361.28]] quas dubio procul non paucas, utut vel obiter saltim in chartam conjectas nec ita\n[[361.29]] plene elaboratas, habet, (sive consistant in terminorum definitionibus et divisionibus, sive in\n[[361.30]] regulis universalibus, sive qualescunque demum aliae sint, quibus propositum in Jurisprudentiae\n[[361.31]] methodo sua catalogum desideratorum minuere tentaverit) nonnulla mecum communicare,\n[[361.32]] eoque ipso ad melius intelligenda verba vestra, stylumque vestrum concisum magis penetrandum,\n[[361.33]] lumen mihi quodpiam accendere haut dedignetur. </p>\n<p> [[362.1]] Equidem, Vir Excellentissime, quemadmodum jam antea impetrandae rei quam maxime\n[[362.2]] desideratae aliquam mihi spem fecisti; ita facilius, credo, spem istam impleturus esses, si mihi\n[[362.3]] isthic loci aliquantisper commorari liceret. Verum meae novercae (quod nomen perquam in jure\n[[362.4]] nostro odiosum novimus) premor odiis et persecutionibus, liteque per eandem de haereditatis,\n[[362.5]] ob pie denatum parentem meum, divisione distineor, cujus exitum nec video, nec ita brevi\n[[362.6]] tempore, longe minus quam ante aliquot menses, mihi ausim polliceri, ut adeo res meas pro\n[[362.7]] lubitu disponere prohibear. Quapropter maximo me beneficio immortaliter sibi obstrinxerit\n[[362.8]] Exc. T. si quasdam memorati generis sive lucubrationes sive meditationes subitaneas, vel prout\n[[362.9]] propria manu exaratae exstant, vel saltem per alium descriptas, sine ullo tamen suo incommodo,\n[[362.10]] ad me transmittere dignabitur. Utroque sane casu nullas non leges forte praescribendas,\n[[362.11]] sancte a me servatum iri, recipio. Quamlibet enim meliori manuductione Academica destitutus,\n[[362.12]] illa tantum incesserim via, qua vulgo itur ad Jurisprudentiae sacrarium, non qua eundum erat,\n[[362.13]] eaque multum quidem motus, sed parum promotus fuerim, siquidem praeter alia multa obstacula,\n[[362.14]] non tam judicii res, quam memoriae, qua parum polleo, offendebam: Scriptores tamen\n[[362.15]] juridici quo plus methodi et <greek>ăkribeíaw f</i>ilosophicae in suis sive compendiis sive syntagmatibus\n[[362.16]] adhibuerunt, eo se mihi commendarunt magis. Itaque dici non potest, quam me libellus e\n[[362.17]] divino tuo ingenio profectus, <i>methodum discendae Jurisprudentiae</i> commonstrans, delectaverit,\n[[362.18]] cum primum aliquanto serius mihi innotesceret, quem non legi tantum, sed iterum saepiusque\n[[362.19]] relegi atque perlegi, sic ut toties repetita lectione nova semper ad voluptatem accessio facta, et\n[[362.20]] tamen discendi sitis mea potius excitata quam satiata fuerit. Nihil enim in eo desidero quam\n[[362.21]] brevitatem, qua praecipue in methodo disponendi, summa tantum juris capita delibat, nec ad\n[[362.22]] specialiora descendit, quod ipsum etiamsi eo loco propositi non erat, meo tamen voto sciendique\n[[362.23]] aviditati magis respondisset. Ut autem hactenus, sic in posterum quoque veritas et\n[[362.24]] accuratior rerum cognitio in deliciis erit, cujus assequendae nullam patiar praeterlabi occasionem,\n[[362.25]] ingentem T. Excell^#'a^#'e habiturus gratiam, si, quod omnium optime, quin imo sola potest,\n[[362.26]] voti me aliqua ex parte damnaverit, eoque fine ex chartis suis vel eas saltem, quae pristinos\n[[362.27]] conceptus in definiendis vel juris vel facti terminis exhibent, mihi, easdem auro contra cariores\n[[362.28]] habituro, invidere aut denegare nolit. Quod enim attinet novos libros, subinde prodeuntes,\n[[362.29]] quorum autores quaedam rationalia juris elementa promittunt, plerique parum solidi continent,\n[[362.30]] nec methodo vere scientifica progrediuntur. Causam non reor aliam esse, quam quod res ista\n[[362.31]] nimis multa praerequirat, et ex intimis philoso<greek>f</i>iae penetralibus, quo tamen paucissimis pertingere\n[[362.32]] datum est, eruenda veniat atque derivanda. </p>\n<p> [[362.33]] Eliae Schnegassii <i>Compendium juris</i> nondum mihi visum. Mirum hoc? at magis mirum,\n[[362.34]] tota Luneburgensium urbe nullum reperiri bibliopolium, quod curiosis novorum scriptorum\n[[363.1]] indagatoribus frequentare liceat. Cognovi autem ex <i>actis</i> <i>eruditorum</i> Lipsiensibus superioris\n[[363.2]] anni, eundem illum autorem ficto sumtoque sibi nomine Antonii a Mara, tractatum edidisse <i>de\n[[363.3]] concursu creditorum</i> , cujus contenta recensentes Lipsienses, eum jactantiae nimiique rigoris in\n[[363.4]] perstringendis aliorum IC^#'t^#'o^#'r^#'u^#'m et ipsius etiam Ulpiani sententiis arguunt. Vereor itaque ne parem\n[[363.5]] subjecturi sint <greek>ĕpíkrisin</i>, quando forte ad dicti compendii enarrationem pervenerint. </p>\n<p> [[363.6]] Caeterum cum percontando explorare hucusque non potuerim, quo tempore Dn. Waltherus\n[[363.7]] Hanoveram abiturus sit, literas has cum adjuncto libro cuidam affinium meorum tradidi,\n[[363.8]] promittenti, se curaturum, ut per primum quemque aurigam merces eo exportantem, ad locum\n[[363.9]] destinatum perferantur. Quod consilium nec T. Excell^#'a^#'e displiciturum credo. Waltherus ille,\n[[363.10]] quem dicis virum in patria historia praeclare versatum, etiam heic multis judicatur plurimum\n[[363.11]] industriae in rebus historicis posuisse, patentibus ipsi ad istud studium tam privata hospitis\n[[363.12]] quondam sui et Consulis Lyneburgensis, B. Crolovii, libris historicis instructissima, quam\n[[363.13]] publica hujus civitatis bibliotheca; quae cum non exiguam MSC^#'t^#'o^#'r^#'u^#'m copiam complectatur, ipse\n[[363.14]] vero in antiquis monachorum characteribus legendis valde promtus sit, non inidoneus etiam\n[[363.15]] fuisse putandus est invenire quidpiam, quod ad Ducum Brunsvico-Lyneburgicorum jus successionis\n[[363.16]] in Ducatum Lauenburgicum, publico scripto, propediem, ut nonnulli augurantur,\n[[363.17]] lucem visuro, deducendum pertineat faciatque. </p>\n<p> [[363.18]] Quod superest, Excellentiam T. oro atque obtestor, ut pro summa humanitate sua certiorem\n[[363.19]] me reddat, quatenus precibus meis locum relinquere, vel spem mihi factam implere velit,\n[[363.20]] neve interim, si forte cum Dn. Walthero colloqui posthac contigerit, eidem aperiat, quid mihi\n[[363.21]] secum intercedat negotii. Quod posterius postulatum suis non destituitur sane haut contemnendis\n[[363.22]] rationibus. Ita Deus ter O. M. Excellentiam T. bono publico quam diutissime servet\n[[363.23]] incolumem protegatque! </p>\n<p> [[363.24]] Scribebam Lüneburgi d. 1. Decembr. Anno 1690. </p>\n<p> [[363.25]] Excellentiae T. Cultor et admirator obsequiosus Johannes Henricus Pape. </p>\n<p> [[363.26]] Viro Excellentissimo, Amplissimo, Consultissimo Dn. Gothofredo Guilielmo Leibnüzio\n[[363.27]] IC^#'t^#'o Serenissimi Ducis Hanoverani Consiliario Aulico longe meritissimo Patrono atque Fautori\n[[363.28]] meo plurimum devenerando. Hanoverae. Bey H. D. von Ludern Fr. Witwen gegen dem\n[[363.29]] Schlosse über. </p>\n",
  "number": "93.",
  "title": "JOHANN HEINRICH PAPE AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Lüneburg, 1. (11.) Dezember 1690. [92.97.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:93. JOHANN HEINRICH PAPE AN LEIBNIZ Lüneburg, 1. (11.) Dezember 1690. [92.97.] Vir Excellentissime, Amplissime, Consultissime, Patrone omni observantiae cultu suspiciende. O fortunatum diem illum, quo Excellentiam Tuam compellare ac de facie nosse mihi contigit! Cujus quidem felicitatis etsi dudum p...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>